Author: iberianpig <[redacted-email]>
Date:   Sun Oct 18 12:45:52 2026 +0000

    Preserve UTC identity when presenting zoned times
    
    Presenting a time in UTC currently calls getlocal(0). That creates a
    fixed-offset Time, so iso8601 writes +00:00 where Rails' UTC zone writes
    Z. Stored Active Record times reach the same conversion.
    
    Use getutc for UTC zone identities and keep getlocal for other zones.
    Share the conversion across presentation, explicit zone conversion,
    local construction and TimeZone#now. Preserve the configured GMT name
    instead of normalizing it to UTC. Use getutc to leave the input intact.
    
    Compare both parser trees against Rails 8.1.4 across ten zones in winter
    and summer. Cover stored and explicitly zoned times in emitted Ruby,
    fractional precision, fixed-zero controls and input preservation.
    
    Co-Authored-By: GPT-6.1 Sol <[redacted-email]>

